  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GEO: ZEG Tbilisi Storytelling Festival</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ZEG is a cross-disciplinary event that brings together storytellers from various professions, forces people out of their silos and into joint thinking about how we can collaboratively shape narratives for the future.  
The inaugural edition took place in 2019, while the second edition was a one-day program titled ZEG in Focus: Ukraine, planned in response to the Russian invasion of Ukraine in 2022. In 2023 we hosted the first fully-fledged festival since 2019, with three days of &#x2018;in-conversation&#x2019; sessions, panel discussions, networking events, workshops, and walking tours. For ZEG 2024 we plan to take the conversations started in 2023 to the next level with an even more diverse group of speakers which will bring together historians, musicians, chefs, actors, journalists, philosophers, comedians, educators, designers, activists, psychologists, medical practitioners, and tech industry leaders in one room to talk about the issues shaping the future. Notably, with 2024 being an important year for elections all over the world, including Georgia, we plan to organize several important sessions on this subject. This will include bringing several journalists and experts from other countries with scheduled elections to discuss challenges such as election rigging and the acute problem presented by election disinformation.</narrative>
  </description>
